art-recovery\", \"score\": 0.85, \"evidence_class\": \"enactment\", \"evidence\": [\"version 0.3.0.002/evidence/scenarios/S-restart-recovery.json\", \"version 0.3.0.002/evidence/launch/launch-20261121-011030.log\"], \"notes\": \"Real second boot against the durable ledger: 427 rows before, 430 after, roster of 6 personas recovered with art artifacts intact.\" },\n346:    { \"id\": \"S-exchange-import\", \"score\": 0.4, \"evidence_class\": \"enactment\", \"evidence\": [\"version 0.3.0.002/evidence/scenarios/S-exchange-import.json\", \"version 0.3.0.002/app/builtins.py:776\", \"version 0.3.0.002/runtime/scenario/artifacts/exports/pkg-5470fb7017f3.json\"], \"notes\": \"Export leg real (valid meridian.exchange/v1 package, 5 personas/2 needs). Import leg failed — scenario-driver bug: scripts/scenarios.py passes ex.get('path') instead of ex['result']['path'], so the tool received package:None and correctly refused it. fn_import_exchange verified correct in code (accepts path string, clamps certainty ≤0.4, basis import); no exchange:imported rows this run. Outcome, not mechanism, failed — flag as harness defect.\" },\n347:    { \"id\": \"S-defer-publication\", \"score\": 0.9, \"evidence_class\": \"enactment\", \"evidence\": [\"version 0.3.0.002/evidence/scenarios/S-defer-publication.json\", \"version 0.3.0.002/runtime/scenario/artifacts/published/1795241425742-cycle-log.md\"], \"notes\": \"Both legs enacted: ungranted request deferred with the missing __grant__ slot recorded; witnessed grant then allowed a real published artifact. D10 fully demonstrated.\" },\n348:    { \"id\": \"S-chat-invocation\", \"score\": 0.7, \"evidence_class\": \"enactment\", \"evidence\": [\"version 0.3.0.002/evidence/scenarios/S-chat-invocation.json\", \"version 0.3.0.002/evidence/scenarios/archive-C-ConversationArchive.json\"], \"notes\": \"Chat turn served by decision-model-ranked sequential respondents (2 floor admissions, 2 floor-played, distinct characterized replies). intents[] and needIds[] empty on this input — the 'matches one or more tool needs, each distinguishable' half of the scenario wasn't exercised by the chosen text.\" },\n349:    { \"id\": \"S-focused-need\", \"score\": 0.35, \"evidence_class\": \"enactment\", \"evidence\": [\"version 0.3.0.002/evidence/scenarios/S-focused-need.json\"], \"notes\": \"Weakest scenario: transcript is one needId plus a single refinement note. Focus mechanics and conversational slot-filling are not demonstrated; no evidence the need stayed open until fulfillment.\" }\n351:  \"notes\": \"Evidence is genuine run output, not self-asserted: consistent assertion ids/timestamps across JSON transcripts, 430-row scenario ledger with every new namespace populated (ethics:gate 7, set:member 57, comparison:run 2/row 4, connector:run 3, calendar:linked 2, archive:segment, temporal:attention 2, speech:floor-admission/played 4 each), live-HTTP timings (wiki 81/174/243ms), live-ollama characterization, real SAPI voice names. Direction-002 rectifications: F1 ethics gate real and deeper than the mark alone (live wikipedia liveness + maxim:objection refusal); F2 temporal reasoning real (context/linkable/note_for_persona; steward presents findings through a persona); F3 general competition lifecycle real; F5 both canonicals enacted for the first time in the line; F6 FIFO speech floor + sequential respondents; F7 per-persona art + rotated real voices; F8 three connectors end-to-end (wikipedia live, ics, files — rss registered but unevidenced; F8's owner bar of 3 met exactly). F4: all six v0.1-only capabilities delivered or challenged on record (C-ConnectorSet, C-DesktopShell challenges in FEATURES.md). Flags: (1) S-exchange-import import leg failed on a scenario-driver bug — scripts/scenarios.py reads 'path' at the wrong result nesting; one-line driver fix plus rerun would close it; (2) devlog-claimed connectors-F8-verify.json is absent from the build; (3) launch-server.out in .002 is a stale copy referencing .001 paths; (4) probe