nents as tool-as-data DSL / object.verb commands / closed primitive allow-li\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\nt (independently converged) |\n98:| C-SetBuild | Geographic set fulfillment — the machinery under S-list-project |\n99:| C-AgenticProtocol | Tools-invoking-tools protocol |\n100:| C-StewardAsTool | Stewardship as a configurable, assignable tool |\n101:| C-UserFacingPriority | Background work yields to user-facing work (policy direction; scheduler free) |\n102:| C-TemplateDerivedUI | Form/execution-check derivation from templates |\n103:| C-ExplicitPolicies | Explicit thresholds/budgets/retry limits; each value separately reviewable |\n109:| C-HostAuthority | Authoritative host + satellite surfaces; transport/topology free unless an exchange agreement p\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nns it |\n110:| C-DesktopShell | Capable of running as its own application with a separate GUI — capability, not the only allowed\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nmethod; browser display is legitimate, expected-best on satellites |\n111:| C-FullScreen | Ability to display full-screen — held for portability's sake |\n112:| C-InspectionSurfaces | Library/Studio/Storefronts-style organization; labels/layout free |\n113:| C-PresentationGlass | Asset pipeline + portrait frames + ambient motion |\n114:| C-ConversationArchive | Per-turn archive + topic segments |\n115:| C-HonestyBanner | Runtime surfaces declare capability honestly (ledger durability, engine/stub status) |\n116:| C-DeclaredStubs | Failed/stubbed capability is declared honestly — no ok:true-while-failing, no silent degradatio\u001b[0mn\u001b[0m\n |\n117:| C-LauncherTests | Bench/owner tests via launcher shortcuts with env baked; owner-facing test steps use operator s\u001b[0mu\u001b[0m\nrfaces only |\n118:| C-DeclaredPresentation | Presentation decisions (typography, palette, alignment, spacing/margins, borders) resolv\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n through a declared common choice set recorded as ledger assertions; interface code consults it at render; embedded pre\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\nentation literals require a recorded challenge |\n119:| C-SettingsPreloads | Named settings preloads as assertion bundles over the common choice set; a preload supplies \u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\ntarting values that later choices supersede; shipped, custom, and exchanged bundles are one kind of object |\n120:| C-SurfaceAssignment | Personalities assignable to specific surfaces |\n121:| C-PresenceRoster | Selectable per-device roster supporting reordering via dyadic relationship assertions by defau\u001b[0ml\u001b[0m\nt |\n122:| C-PresenceStage | Stage showing current-discussion participants and shows; traversal via scripted paths where the\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\ndisplay allows |\n123:| C-QuickSelect | Quick-select control near chat |\n124:| C-ChorusOnAddress | Chorus members of any rank appear when directly addressed |\n130:| C-PerceivableRespondents | Respondent contributions remain individually perceivable; overlapping speech that rend\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\nrs them indistinct requires a recorded challenge |\n131:| C-SequentialRespondents | Multiple respondents present in sequence, each able to react to earlier contributions |\n===SWEEP===\n# Convention reclassification sweep — 2026-11-19\n\nPer owner ruling 3 in `conventions-001.md`: every D-* record and every review finding\nclassified across the three-layer model — **prompt** (specified behavior — \"requirement\"\nis not a defined corpus term; the prompt needs none), **convention** (challengeable,\nnever ignorable — recorded departure required), **implementation choice** (free), or\n**harness** (evaluation machinery). Recommendations pending owner adoption.\n\n## D-* records\n\n| Record | Proposed class | Explanation |\n|--------|---------------|-------------|\n| D-ProductNaming | implementation choice | The record itself says independent implementations choose names; A12 concer\u001b[0mn\u001b[0m\n is owner-visible but doesn't make naming conventional |\n| D-PersistentLocalIndices | **C-LocalIndices** | Stable local indices for persistent objects is a proven, converged pa\u001b[0mt\u001b[0m\ntern (avatarID/toolID); labels and encoding free — prompt already specifies the durable-identity behavior |\n| D-DyadicNormalization | **C-DyadicConfidence** | Shared normalization gives independent builds comparable confidence \u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\nemantics and threshold discipline; math details challengeable |\n| D-CertaintyPrivilege | split | **User-set supremacy: C-UserSetSupremacy** — briefly ruled prompt-level then reclassif\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\ned convention per owner rulings 2026-11-19. Dyadic-top + recency mechanics: **C-CertaintyPrivilege** |\n| D-ResponseDepth | implementation choice | Record itself marks conversational dynamics implementation work; user-facin\u001b[0mg\u001b[0m\n depth control is one realization among others |\n| D-LedgerStorage | **C-JsonlLedger** (seeded) | Independently converged in GreyAvatar and Meridian — strongest convent\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\non evidence |\n| D-TemplatesAndWorkshops | **C-TemplateDerivedUI** | Form/execution-check derivation from templates converged in both \u001b[0mb\u001b[0m\nuilds (Meridian: derived workshop forms) |\n| D-HostAndSurfaces | **C-HostAuthority** | Authoritative host + satellite surfaces is a proven topology; transport/top\u001b[0mo\u001b[0m\nlogy free unless an exchange agreement pins it |\n| D-SpeechScheduling | **C-SpeechFloor** | Serialized playback admission — the convention that would have prevented v0.\u001b[0m3\u001b[0m\n's overlapping-voices failure. The floor itself is C-PerceivableRespondents (P2 reclassified convention); the queue/FIF\u001b[0mO\u001b[0m\n manner is this convention |\n| D-IdleTurnAsTool | **C-StewardAsTool** | Stewardship as a configurable, assignable tool — converged (Meridian: config\u001b[0mu\u001b[0m\nrable steward thread) |\n| D-BackgroundThrottling | **C-UserFacingPriority** | The *policy direction* (background yields to user-facing) is conv\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\nntional; scheduler mechanism is free; the responsiveness outcome is already prompt-required |\n| D-EngineMapping | **C-EngineMapping** | Portable preferences vs device mapping separation is a proven seam (AVQR voic\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n guide); engine selection free |\n| D-ExchangeEncoding | **C-ExchangeLayers** + contract note | **Owner correction 2026-11-19: this is layered, not singl\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n** — multiple encoding layers and channels (2D-barcode encode *and* read is itself a big step; AVQR, codebooks, envelop\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\ns, printed budgets, postcard batch are separate layers). An adopted schema pins provisionally within its layer (evolvin\u001b[0mg\u001b[0m\n over time; revocable through the schema's own process); departure always available by not claiming the schema — you ca\u001b[0mn\u001b[0m\n't claim the contract while breaking it |\n| D-InterfaceOrganization | **C-InspectionSurfaces** | Library/Studio/Storefronts organization is a proven UX pattern; \u001b[0ml\u001b[0m\nabels/layout free |\n| D-FixedPolicies | **C-ExplicitPolicies** | The pattern of explicit thresholds/budgets/retry limits is conventional; e\u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\nch value separately reviewable |\n| D-UnmetNeedRecords | **C-UnmetNeedRecords** | Converged in both builds (Meridian: unmet-need floor); record-shape det\u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\nils replaceable |\n| D-ResponseAcceptanceEncoding | **C-AcceptanceChecks** | Executable adequacy checks + candidate retention + confidence\u001b[0m-\u001b[0m\nlowering is the proven seam; regex encoding free |\n| D-ToolMatchingByRegex | split | Regex itself: implementation choice (record says so). The deterministic-match *plus* \u001b[0mL\u001b[0m\nLM-review pairing: **C-DeterministicMatchReview** convention candidate |\n| D-ToolTrustChurn | prompt-side | The rank-adjustment behavior is shortcoming A5 — prompt material, not convention (re\u001b[0mc\u001b[0m\nord itself: implemented incorrectly = defect). Mechanics free |\n| D-SourceConfidenceCeilings | **C-SourceCeilings** | Per-source confidence ceilings are a proven realization. Mixed-re\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\nults review — mechanism corrected per owner 2026-11-19: **records are immutable; values are never changed, newer entrie\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\n are derived and used, creating the audit trail** (already prompt-required semantics: corrections add assertions). The \u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\neview loop's own classification stays flagged for the prompt pass |\n| D-SourceRelevanceDomains | **C-SourceDomains** | Domain-described sources is a proven realization; vocabulary/matchin\u001b[0mg\u001b[0m\n free |\n| D-StructuredSpecialtySearch | split per owner 2026-11-19 | Multi-source access capability → **C-MultiSourceAccess** (\u001b[0mP\u001b[0m\n5 reclassified convention). **Conventions:** **C-CompetingSources** (Wikipedia and Google as separate competitors); **C\u001b[0m-\u001b[0m\nSpecializedListRetrieval** (evaluating specialized over general search for list completion — the machinery behind S-lis\u001b[0mt\u001b[0m\n-project's defensible answers); **C-ConfiguredAccounts** (gmail, calendar, profiles access); **C-ContactTags** (ledger \u001b[0mt\u001b[0m\nags for contacts) |\n| D-DevelopmentHarness | outside sweep | Governing process realization — lives in the harness layer, not the product sp\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\nc layers |\n\n## F-entry classification\n\n| Finding | Class | Explanation |\n|---------|-------|-------------|"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
