{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've figured out how to interpret the convention conformance tables, mapping their states to `conformed`, `reckoned-departure`, or `silent-departure`. Silent departures are tricky; I'll only mark them if explicitly stated, otherwise, I'll rely on the build's table and verdict JSON. Unchecked IDs represent gaps. Now that I have a clear understanding, I can proceed with the design and implementation."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:20.889519500+00:00"}}}}
