{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm reconsidering the layout for the shell and emitter scripts. The emitter should deploy the shell into each project's `display/` directory and write `data.js`. The version folder should contain the emitter and the master copy of the shell. Placing the shell source within the version folder (`version/.../shell/`) and having the emitter accept a `-ShellDir` parameter, defaulting to a relative path, seems most robust. This approach also aligns with a potential future mirroring to a central template directory. The fleet index page will use the same shell, populated by fleet-wide summary data in `data.js`."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:24.352339300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe project page `display/index.html` loads `data.js`, which contains the project payload. This payload can be either a \"fleet\" or \"project\" kind. The fleet payload includes a list of projects, each with details like ID, path, name, budget, and last verdict. The project payload is more detailed, including state information, build history, scenario suites, convention matrices, and liveness data."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:27.646192600+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-23T23:28:31.048066Z  INFO chisel_agent::skills_loading: skills discovery: cwd=C:\builds\harness-ui workspace_root=C:\builds additional_dirs=1 providers=[devin,agents_standard,cursor,windsurf,claude,opencode,zed,copilot,codex,kiro] scanned_scopes=3 loaded=49 by_provider=[builtin=3,cursor=7,devin=39] errors=0
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm parsing the devlog to extract version entries, verdicts, and associated JSON blocks. For the comparison chart, I'll use ordered verdict blocks as columns, labeled by entry and a suffix (e.g., \"C1\", \"C1-rescore\"). Cycle timestamps will be derived from entry headings and time-to-implement fields. The convention matrix will consolidate IDs from various sources and populate cells based on FEATURES.md tables and verdict JSON, marking absent conventions visibly."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:31.134271400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm defining the scenario matrix by combining suite IDs from `.devin/scenarios.md` with those in verdict scenario arrays, marking missing entries as gaps. The launch pointer will highlight the most recent build's `launch.cmd` or equivalent, with older builds marked as stale. Liveness checks will exclude `display/`, `.devin/`, and `.git/` directories, and potentially emitted files like `index.html`. Emitter parameters are being finalized, with `-Once` defaulting when `-Watch` is absent, and each `-Watch` iteration will include a scan. Discovery logic targets folders containing `.devin/` or `devlog.md`. The shell rendering is minimal, loading `data.js` and `harness.js` which then dynamically renders fleet or project views."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:35.149759200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm planning a refresh mechanism using `setInterval` to inject a script tag with a timestamped source, triggering a re-render if the data is newer. On focus or visibility change, I'll check for updates but only re-render if the timestamp is newer. I'll implement a `loadData` function to handle script injection and re-rendering logic. For the chart, I'm considering a hand-rolled SVG line chart, with per-criterion coloring, sparse data handling, and a depth picker. Points will be clickable to build a detail view. Missing data will be shown as '—' with styling and tooltips, and whole-section gaps will display a \"gap\" panel. For render-checking, I'll investigate using headless browsers like `msedge` to dump the DOM and then grep it for expected element counts, writing the results to a file."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:39.768347400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I have the full picture now. Let me check what runtimes are available for the emitter (PowerShell version) and the render-check (headless browser / python / node)."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:39.776509100+00:00"}}}}
