{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm setting up the project structure, including the emitter script, shell files, and launcher artifacts. The emitter logic needs to be compatible with PowerShell 5.1, so I'll avoid newer syntax like `??` and be mindful of `ConvertFrom-Json` limitations. I'll parse project discovery, devlog entries, and state files, associating verdicts by their position relative to entry headings and JSON blocks."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:48.102625800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm determining how to track convention dispositions by parsing convention tables and identifying relevant IDs from corpus and scenario files. I'll also establish liveness based on file modification times, excluding specific directories. For output, I'll generate HTML, JavaScript, and CSS files for both individual projects and a fleet overview, ensuring data is serialized correctly using PowerShell's `ConvertTo-Json`. Logging will be timestamped and directed to a file within an evidence directory."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:52.004847+00:00"}}}}
2026-11-23T23:28:52.056286Z  INFO connect_post{path="/exa.product_analytics_pb.ProductAnalyticsService/BatchRecordAnalyticsEvents"}: connect_rpc::client: close time.busy=141µs time.idle=56.7ms
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm structuring the UI around four tabs: Summary, Comparison, Current State, and Builds. The Summary tab will display state.json fields, pending questions, and a gap panel for missing state.json, alongside verbatim status files. Comparison will feature an SVG chart, depth picker, and scenario/convention matrices. Current State shows live corpus IDs, prompt revisions, and snapshot comparisons. Builds will list builds with a detail panel for selected items, including timestamps, verdict JSON, evidence citations, and the latest launch pointer. Data will reload every 30 seconds, with checks also triggered by visibility changes and focus events, comparing `generated_at` timestamps to re-render only when newer. A \"last checked / data stamp\" indicator and a ticking liveness age will be displayed. I'm also running the emitter once against C:\\builds, logging to evidence/scan-<ts>.log, and deploying harness-ui's display, noting that harness-ui will show honest gaps due to an empty builds array and no verdicts."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:56.238198200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm performing a render check using Edge's `--headless --dump-dom` on two HTML files to capture their DOM structures. I'll then compare the row counts in these dumped DOMs against the source files to identify discrepancies. I'll also try the `--headless=new` flag if the current command fails. Finally, I'll record build details in a manifest and map scenario enactments to evidence in a separate notes file."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:28:59.258285500+00:00"}}}}
