{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#aeb045941c664bc8b3abee672c91ddc3","status":"in_progress","_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/cwd":"C:\\builds\\harness-ui"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#aeb045941c664bc8b3abee672c91ddc3","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"# Project Prompt\n\nDevelop an independent implementation of a private, local-first ecosystem in which a persistent assertion ledger record\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\n semantic state, distinct personalities interpret that shared ledger through their own lenses, configurable tools perfo\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nm useful work, and locally controlled devices provide capabilities and surfaces for the user. The implementation may us\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n any programming language, architecture, model provider, storage arrangement, or interface method that preserves the be\u001b[0mh\u001b[0m\navior below.\n\n## Purpose and scope\n\nThe system exists to benefit its user through useful local agency. Its goals include reducing dependence on provider se\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nvices, lowering the cost of useful agentic work, and helping the beneficiary consider — or, when authorized, automate —\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nevaluation of their own best interests.\n\nThe user is the party the installation serves; audiences and interlocutors may interact with an installation without be\u001b[0mc\u001b[0m\noming its user, as when a public installation serves visitors on behalf of an operating organization.\n\nThe default target is a private installation on physically local, user-controlled devices. A local network may connect \u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\neveral devices and surfaces. The installation may coordinate different local models, tools, and input/output devices, b\u001b[0mu\u001b[0m\nt hardware assignment and model distribution are implementation choices. Remote services and broader federation are opt\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nonal integrations or exchange paths, not requirements of the default installation.\n\n## Assertion ledger"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#aeb045941c664bc8b3abee672c91ddc3","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"# Project Prompt\n\nDevelop an independent implementation of a private, local-first ecosystem in which a persistent assertion ledger record\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\n semantic state, distinct personalities interpret that shared ledger through their own lenses, configurable tools perfo\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nm useful work, and locally controlled devices provide capabilities and surfaces for the user. The implementation may us\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n any programming language, architecture, model provider, storage arrangement, or interface method that preserves the be\u001b[0mh\u001b[0m\navior below.\n\n## Purpose and scope\n\nThe system exists to benefit its user through useful local agency. Its goals include reducing dependence on provider se\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nvices, lowering the cost of useful agentic work, and helping the beneficiary consider — or, when authorized, automate —\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nevaluation of their own best interests.\n\nThe user is the party the installation serves; audiences and interlocutors may interact with an installation without be\u001b[0mc\u001b[0m\noming its user, as when a public installation serves visitors on behalf of an operating organization.\n\nThe default target is a private installation on physically local, user-controlled devices. A local network may connect \u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\neveral devices and surfaces. The installation may coordinate different local models, tools, and input/output devices, b\u001b[0mu\u001b[0m\nt hardware assignment and model distribution are implementation choices. Remote services and broader federation are opt\u001b[0mi\u001b[0m\nonal integrations or exchange paths, not requirements of the default installation.\n\n## Assertion ledger\n\nThe assertion ledger is the book of record for persistent semantic application state. A user input becomes a typed, att\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nibuted assertion. Assertions retain their source, typed value, certainty, provenance, time, and relationships to later \u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\nssertions. Contextual confidence ranks applicability separately from the assertion's certainty. Computed views, caches,\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\npayload stores, and segmented files may support the implementation, but they remain subordinate to the ledger and do no\u001b[0mt\u001b[0m\n become a second descriptive truth store."}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
