{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm struggling with how to implement the `-Watch` parameter in PowerShell. The spec requires supporting both a bare `-Watch` (implying a 30-second interval) and `-Watch <seconds>`, but PowerShell's parameter binding makes this difficult. A switch parameter (`[switch]$Watch`) can't accept an argument, and making `-Watch` an integer (`[int]$Watch`) would cause errors if passed without a value. I'm considering a few options, including using a sentinel value like `-1` for the integer parameter or a combination of `[switch]$Watch` and `[int]$Interval`, but I need to ensure the literal `-Watch <seconds>` form is honored."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:29:32.181151700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI've decided to implement the `-Watch` parameter using `[int]$Watch = -1` as a sentinel value. This allows `-Watch 45` to work as expected, `-Watch 0` to default to 30 seconds (as documented), and a bare `-Watch` to trigger PowerShell's own error message, fulfilling the spec's signature. I'll also update the help comment to clarify the `-Watch 0` default."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:29:36.534472800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm parsing build output, extracting labels, dates, and verdict lists with JSON. I also need to capture the full text of \"Result:\" fields for evidence citations, potentially capping them at 4000 characters. For builds, I'm prioritizing version sorting over modification time, using a regex to extract version numbers and falling back to mtime if needed."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:29:40.929956500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm parsing convention tables from FEATURES.md, mapping disposition text to standardized states like 'conformed' or 'reckoned-departure'. I'll also merge convention data from verdict JSON and handle potential errors when parsing state.json. Additionally, I'm extracting scenario IDs and text from scenarios.md and reading raw status text from .devin/last-*-status.txt files."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:29:44.497551600+00:00"}}}}
