{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm setting up a comparison of rendered elements against their source representations, logging counts for fleet rows, criteria points, scenario cells, and convention IDs. For headless Edge testing, I'll use `--headless=new --dump-dom` and `--virtual-time-budget` to capture evidence of stale-refresh enactments, noting that `file://` script loads might still function. I'll also document the focus-reload logic."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:30:04.849527200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `state.json` schema currently only records revision strings, not full ID sets. To accurately track staleness, I can compare the live scenario ID set against the set recorded in the last verdict. This diff reveals unassessed scenarios. Similarly, convention IDs in `FEATURES.md` can be compared against those in the corpus's `CONVENTIONS.md` to find unassessed conventions, without needing new fields in `state.json`."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:30:07.423380500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm enacting liveness checks by scanning files, then touching specific files in `stalerig/display/` and `.devin/` to prove liveness isn't reset by those directories. The scan logs themselves will serve as evidence, recording `liveness_seconds` per project. I'll start writing files with the emitter script, keeping track of line counts for `devin`."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:30:08.358655300+00:00"}}}}
