{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm seeing a few issues. The `-f` operator in `Write-Log` seems fine with backslashes, but I'm double-checking the `(\"{0}\\{1}\" -f ...)` pattern. For bullet checks, the order of `'Criteria'` and `'Criteria (rubric revision)'` matters; my current check handles both. Strict mode complains about `$script:section` being referenced before assignment, but it's actually assigned first, so it should work. Entry kind detection using `'^version\\s'` seems correct for parsing versions and labels. `ConvertTo-Json -Depth 40` is fine for PS 5.1, and `ConvertFrom-Json` should handle duplicate keys. Finally, the liveness exclusion matches the spec."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:31:05.403823700+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm confirming that `-Depth` works in PowerShell 5.0, but I'm removing it as I'm changing the path anyway. Entries without verdicts don't contribute to the corpus, but build details can still show the cycle. For `last_verdict`, `$null -ne $sp.verdict.overall` correctly handles missing properties. The `Values` property of an ordered dictionary works with `Select-Object -First 1`. My regex for convention table headers correctly handles `C-` prefixes, and the `C-\\*` pattern correctly matches literal `C-*` entries. The row parse regex is also correct for convention IDs. I'll fix the emitter with edits to version key computation, sorting, corpus derivation, and latest fix."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:31:13.410540400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"Two bugs to fix in the emitter: unconditional corpus-id seeding (would wrongly attribute `C:\\Project` conventions to harness-ui) and fragile version sorting. Editing now."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:31:13.410788200+00:00"}}}}
