{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm deciding how to render the state. If `state.json` is missing, I'll show a \"state.json missing\" gap. Otherwise, I'll display the state's keys, nesting objects as tables or JSON. I'll explicitly show `direction_in_force` details, `pending_owner_questions` (or a gap if absent), and `builds[]` (or \"none recorded\"). For comparisons, I'll use a depth picker for series data, create an SVG chart with polylines and circles, and potentially add user opinions as hollow diamonds. I'll also render scenario and convention matrices, using gaps for missing data."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:32:10.518255600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm mapping build details to series entries, which simplifies the UI. The left column will list series labels, showing timestamps, verdict JSON, evidence citations, and a launch pointer. If a build is missing, it'll show a gap; older builds will be marked as stale. Clicking a chart selection will update the verdict index and switch tabs."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:32:13.224128300+00:00"}}}}
