{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm reconsidering the error's location. If \"project: project\" didn't print, the error must be within `fleetRows.Add` or its loop iteration, not in `Invoke-Scan` after the loop. The `fleetRows.Add` call uses `$data.state`, and I'm checking if `$data.status_files` could be null or empty, causing `fleetRows.Add` to bind a null path. However, `$data.status_files.Count` being zero is handled, and `OrderedDictionary.Values` exists. The `Copy-Item` and `Write-TextFile` calls after the loop also seem fine."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:34:36.679786200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm improving error handling by adding a `trap` within the script to capture the specific position of an error. The previous `try/catch` block only reported the error's line number as 1 because the exception was propagated. By setting `$ErrorActionPreference` and printing `$error[0].InvocationInfo` after the `trap`, I expect to get the correct line number and script context directly from the exception record's `InvocationInfo`."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:34:37.608449600+00:00"}}}}
