{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I'm seeing a recurring issue with backslash escapes in Python strings, specifically with `\\P` and `\\b`. It seems like `\\\\P` in a heredoc is correctly interpreted as `\\P`, but a warning suggests a single backslash appeared. Similarly, `\\\\b` in a triple-quoted string should resolve to `\\b`, but the `Get-Item` command is failing as if it's a backspace character. I need to trace where these single backslashes are actually originating."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:45:28.070427300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nWait, the error `The property 'FullName' cannot be found on this object` at `return [ordered]@{` seems to stem from `$pd` being a string like 'C:\\builds\\project', not a DirectoryInfo object. But then the log shows \"corpus: prompt ref none derivable,\" which implies `Get-Item` might have failed due to a mangled path, resulting in `$pd` being null. If `$pd` was null, `$projDir.FullName` would throw immediately, but the log shows it parsed *some* devlog. The output is truncated, so the actual devlog parsing might have succeeded on the real project."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:45:30.293723400+00:00"}}}}
