{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe `$d.Keys` call is failing because `$d` is an error object, not a dictionary. This seems to be a consequence of `Build-ProjectData` throwing an error partway through. Even with `ErrorActionPreference='Continue'`, the strict error on `$projDir.FullName` isn't terminating as expected, which is causing the subsequent partial construction of the ordered dictionary and complicating error handling."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:45:32.186104400+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nWait — the `Build-ProjectData` function is failing because `$pd` is a string, not a `DirectoryInfo` object. This suggests `Get-Item` failed, possibly due to a mangled path like `'C:\\builds\\project'`. The Python heredoc warning about `\\P` might be a red herring; the real issue seems to be how the path is being passed to `Get-Item` or how `Build-ProjectData` is receiving it."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:45:32.962503800+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nWait, the error `property FullName cannot be found` suggests `$projDir` is a string, not a `DirectoryInfo` object. But if `Get-Item` failed earlier, `$projDir` would be null, causing a different error. The log shows the function ran and parsed *some* devlog, implying `$projDir` was an object, but one lacking `FullName`. This points to `$pd` being passed as a string to `Build-ProjectData`, which then fails to create a proper `DirectoryInfo` object."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:45:35.355155100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe serialization hang persists after the corpus log, and `ConvertTo-Json` is the likely culprit. I'm considering a custom `ToJson` function using `System.Text.Json` or hand-rolled emission to bypass `ConvertTo-Json`'s overhead and potential quirks, especially since the payload schema is controlled. Before that, I'll test if `ConvertFrom-Json` is creating oversized objects. I also suspect a subtle issue with how OrderedDictionary handles property assignment versus key addition in `$d.verdict = 'x'`, which might be the root cause."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:45:37.092258300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm writing a custom JSON serializer in PowerShell. It handles nulls, booleans, strings, characters, numbers, dates, dictionaries, and enumerables. For .NET objects, it serializes public properties. I've also included a `JsonEscape` function to handle special characters and control codes."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:45:39.746874100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nRather than fight `ConvertTo-Json` quirks, I'll hand-roll the serializer — deterministic, fast, and the verdict stays verbatim. Replacing it: numbers (`[ValueType]`) are handled, but enums need casting to int. Datetime checks precede `ValueType` checks. For doubles, I'll use invariant culture formatting like `'r'` or `'g17'`, and integral types will use `ToString()`. PSObject fallbacks handle nested PSCustomObjects and hashtables, ensuring only `$data.state` remains. Null properties will serialize as 'null'."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:45:45.544108600+00:00"}}}}
