{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"The process is still hanging after emitting project display, specifically during `fleetRows.Add`. The log doesn't show \"fleet serialize start,\" suggesting the issue might be buffered output or a problem with `Get-ChildItem` on the root directory. I'm now considering if the hang is with the shell execution pipe rather than the process itself, as CPU usage is still climbing, indicating a loop. I'm investigating potential infinite enumerations in `foreach` loops, especially with `DataTable` or string inputs."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:48:38.752652600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe payload structure doesn't seem to contain heavy objects like `DirectoryInfo` that would explain the CPU burn. The `ConvertTo-JsonEscape` regex callback on large strings is a potential culprit, but the project payload serialized quickly. This suggests the hang occurs *after* project emission, during the fleet stage, despite the data not appearing computationally intensive."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:48:41.685293600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm investigating a hang between emitting project display and fleet emission. The code shows `fleetRows.Add` using `[ordered]@{}.Values`, which returns an `OrderedDictionaryValueCollection`. I'm checking if `Select-Object -First 1` on this collection could be the bottleneck, though `.Count` on `ArrayList` and `OrderedDict` values seem fine."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:48:44.898109600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI can't see the problem with the current output, so I'll run it to a file to watch the progress. A simpler fix than modifying `Invoke-Scan` to write incrementally would be to have `Write-Log` append directly to the log file, which would also prevent hangs."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:48:45.404451600+00:00"}}}}
