{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've found the issue with the `series null` labels for the reference builds. My regex for extracting version numbers from headings was too greedy. It was capturing only '0' from 'version 0.1' because `\\S+` stops at the first space. I need to adjust it to `version\\s+([0-9][0-9.]*)` to correctly capture the full version number, like '0.1'."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:51:17.969193100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI've identified an issue with how I'm labeling rescores. My regex for detecting \"Re-score verdict\" was too strict, requiring an exact match for \"**Re-score verdict**\" and failing because the actual text includes a colon, \"**Re-score verdict:**\". This also affected the \"Verdict\" detection. The rescore case incorrectly fell back to a generic label, and a second primary verdict would also be mislabeled. I need to adjust the regexes to be more flexible, like matching `Re-score\\s+verdict` and `\\*\\*Verdict`, and ensure the \"Re-score\" check happens before the general \"Verdict\" check."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:51:19.101191300+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm seeing a discrepancy in how fleet rows handle missing state. For one project, the `direction` field is correctly null because the state is absent, which is honest. However, for harness-ui, the `verdict` is null, but my JS logic shows \"no parsed verdict\" while the fleet JS shows \"—\". This suggests an inconsistency in how null verdicts are handled. Also, `series null` entries show 12 scenarios, but the label is broken; I need to fix the label regex. Finally, the 'C1.2' series should be 'C1-rescore'."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:51:20.853753400+00:00"}}}}
