{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"It looks like the `$Matches` variable is being reset by the second `-match` operation within the `Parse-Devlog` function. When processing reference builds, the `^version\\s` pattern matches, but it has no capturing groups. This overwrites `$Matches` with only the matched string (`version `), causing `$Matches[1]` to become null. For cycle entries, this second match fails, so `$Matches` retains the correct heading from the initial `###` match. The fix is to capture the heading into a separate variable before the second match."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:51:37.640364+00:00"}}}}
