{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"Backslash escaping is fixed, so JSON now correctly parses `C:\\\\Project\\\\...` to `C:\\Project\\...`. I'm double-checking the `data.js` validity, as the raw JSON is injected verbatim and parsed by Node's `eval`. Fleet row checks are good: project direction is null (no `state.json`), and harness-ui direction is `direction-001.md (signed)`. Scenario enactment evidence looks solid, with the fixture run emitting to the correct directory. However, the liveness check shows all fixture files were just written, making their age minimal, which might skew the staleness results."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:52:49.004591100+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm setting up a demonstration for the \"growing age\" and \"reset on write\" features. To show \"growing age,\" I'll initially set fixture mtimes to an old date (2026-11-01) to create a large age, then touch an excluded file to ensure the age remains large, and finally touch an in-scope file to reset the age to near zero. This sequence should clearly demonstrate the S-liveness-age behavior. I also need to verify that `brokenrig` correctly handles missing `state.json` and suite/launcher information, resulting in expected gaps in the output."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:52:49.912764100+00:00"}}}}
