{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"_cognition.ai/compaction","params":{"status":"completed","summary":"Full conversation history saved at C:\\Users\\kris_\\AppData\\Roaming\\devin\\cli\\summaries\\history_0d54bb4357a04533.md.\nSummary:\n<summary>\n1. Request and Intent:\n\n   The user initiated a fresh build session for `harness-ui`, a development-harness status display line under `C:\\builds\\harness-ui`, governed by `direction-001.md` and the embedded `prompt.md` snapshot.\n\n   Enduring objective: build a read-only, file-derived status display over a builds root, defaulting to `C:\\builds`, that works directly from `file://` without a server, network access, or runtime dependencies beyond vendored/static files. It must derive status from existing harness artifacts rather than accepting session-reported status, and must render missing or unparsed information honestly as visible gaps. The intended end state is a dogfooded harness display that can later be mirrored into `C:\\Harness\\harness\\templates\\display/`.\n\n   The explicit user request was to realize the entire application for direction-001 as the first fresh build:\n   - Produce `version 0.1.0.001/`.\n   - Include the PowerShell emitter, static shell, vendored dependencies, emitted artifacts, and evidence.\n   - Run the emitter for real against `C:\\builds`, using the real `C:\\builds\\project` corpus as the test corpus.\n   - Update Cycle 1 in `devlog.md` with the result and implementation time, but do not fill the Verdict because a separate judge session owns that field.\n\n   The implementation work progressed through:\n   - Reading `AGENTS.md`, `direction-001.md`, `prompt.md`, `.devin/scenarios.md`, `state.json`, and `devlog.md`.\n   - Inspecting the real `C:\\builds\\project` corpus, including its devlog, builds, scenario suite, evidence, launch artifacts, and absence of `.devin/state.json`.\n   - Creating the build structure and emitter.\n   - Creating the static shell and CSS/JS.\n   - Creating fixture projects for honest-absence, stale-data, liveness, and launch-pointer scenarios.\n   - Debugging PowerShell parsing, serialization, strict-mode property access, and verdict-label derivation.\n   - Running the emitter successfully against `C:\\builds`.\n   - Running headless Edge checks against fleet, project summary, comparison, current-state, and build-detail views.\n   - The session had not yet completed the final manifest/devlog update or fully resolved the latest JSON escaping patch attempt.\n\n2. Key Concepts and Values:\n\n   Technical concepts:\n   - Static HTML/JavaScript shell loaded via `file://`.\n   - PowerShell emitter with `-Once` and `-Watch <seconds>`.\n   - `window.HARNESS_DATA = {...}` payloads.\n   - Cache-busted script reload rather than `fetch()`, because `fetch()` is blocked under `file://`.\n   - Fleet discovery based on directories containing both `.devin/` and `devlog.md`.\n   - Devlog fenced JSON verdict extraction.\n   - `.devin/state.json` state snapshots.\n   - `.devin/scenarios.md` scenario IDs.\n   - `FEATURES.md` convention tables.\n   - Current-state live corpus reads.\n   - Liveness derived from newest in-scope file mtime.\n   - Hand-rolled SVG chart rendering.\n   - Sparse per-criterion comparison lines.\n   - Scenario/convention matrices with explicit gaps.\n   - Build-detail launch pointers restricted to the latest build.\n   - Honest absence and visible gap rendering.\n   - Headless Edge DOM checks.\n   - PowerShell 5.1 compatibility and UTF-8 BOM handling.\n\n   Required views:\n   - Fleet index.\n   - Project summary.\n   - Comparison.\n   - Current state.\n   - Build detail.\n\n   Important paths:\n   - Workspace: `C:\\builds\\harness-ui`\n   - Project root: `C:\\builds\\project`\n   - Builds root: `C:\\builds`\n   - Build output: `C:\\builds\\harness-ui\\version 0.1.0.001`\n   - Emitter: `version 0.1.0.001\\emitter\\harness-emit.ps1`\n   - Shell source files:\n     - `version 0.1.0.001\\shell\\index.html`\n     - `version 0.1.0.001\\shell\\harness.js`\n     - `version 0.1.0.001\\shell\\styles.css`\n   - Evidence directory: `version 0.1.0.001\\evidence`\n   - Fixture directory: `version 0.1.0.001\\fixtures`\n   - Deployed project shell: `C:\\builds\\harness-ui\\display`\n   - Deployed fleet files: `C:\\builds\\index.html`, `C:\\builds\\data.js`\n   - Deployed real project payload: `C:\\builds\\project\\display\\data.js`\n   - Corpus prompt: `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\ProjectPrompt.md`\n   - Corpus conventions: `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`\n\n   Real corpus observations:\n   - `C:\\builds` contains `harness-ui` and `project`.\n   - `project` has four version folders: `version 0.3.0.001` through `version 0.3.0.004`.\n   - `project` has 26 scenarios and 56 convention IDs from the corpus.\n   - `project` has no `.devin/state.json`, intentionally exercising honest absence.\n   - The project devlog contains seven parsed verdict JSON blocks across reference versions and cycles.\n   - Latest real build is `version 0.3.0.004`.\n   - `project` has launch artifacts including `launch.cmd`.\n   - `harness-ui` currently has one Cycle 1 state snapshot with budget spent `1 / 1`, no parsed verdict yet.\n\n   Real emitted payload verification:\n   - Fleet payload kind: `fleet`.\n   - Fleet discovered two projects.\n   - `project` payload contains seven verdict series points, 26 scenarios, 56 convention IDs, four builds, and latest build `version 0.3.0.004`.\n   - Current-state payload correctly reported the corpus prompt and conventions paths.\n   - Comparison rendered 40 SVG points.\n   - Scenario matrix rendered `182` cells with `98` filled.\n   - Convention matrix rendered `224` cells with `196` gaps, confirming visible absence behavior.\n   - Build detail rendered a launch pointer to `../version%200.3.0.004/launch.cmd`.\n   - Current-state view rendered 26 live scenario IDs and 56 live convention IDs.\n\n3. Task Requirements:\n\n   Overall task:\n   - “Scope: realize the entire prompt — a read-only status display over the builds root (default `C:\\builds`), file://-openable, no server, no network, no runtime deps beyond vendored files.”\n   - Produce `version 0.1.0.001/` as a fresh build.\n   - Do not modify project source artifacts such as `devlog.md` or `state.json` during emitter operation; only emitted artifacts, root artifacts, and the emitter’s own run log may be written.\n\n   Emitter:\n   - PowerShell implementation.\n   - `-Once` regenerates every payload and the fleet index.\n   - `-Watch <seconds>` loops, defaulting to 30 seconds.\n   - Scan the builds root for project folders carrying `.devin/` and `devlog.md`.\n   - Emit:\n     - `<root>/index.html`\n     - `<root>/data.js`\n     - Each project’s `display/data.js`.\n   - Use `window.HARNESS_DATA = {...}` payloads.\n   - Parse:\n     - `devlog.md`\n     - `.devin/state.json`\n     - `.devin/scenarios.md`\n     - `.devin/last-*-status.txt`\n     - build folders\n     - verdict JSON from devlog fenced blocks, with raw `.devin/jev-cycle-*.out` as fallback where applicable\n     - `FEATURES.md` convention tables\n   - Compute liveness as seconds since newest in-scope mtime, excluding:\n     - `display/`\n     - `.devin/` internals\n     - `.git/`\n   - Read current convention/scenario IDs and prompt revision from the configured corpus.\n   - Log discovered projects, parsed files, extracted verdicts, and exclusions.\n   - Ensure `-Once` completes reliably on Windows PowerShell 5.1.\n\n   Static shell:\n   - Provide `index.html` and JavaScript shell.\n   - Must work from a cold checkout via `file://`.\n   - Must not rely on `fetch()`.\n   - Reload `data.js` using a cache-busted script tag.\n   - Poll every 30 seconds while visible.\n   - On refocus, reload only when the generated-at stamp is newer.\n   - Use either a vendored single-file chart library or hand-rolled chart rendering; the implementation chose hand-rolled SVG.\n   - Include the shell files in the build and deploy them into project display folders.\n\n   Fleet index:\n   - One row per discovered project.\n   - Show:\n     - line name\n     - direction in force\n     - budget spent\n     - last verdict\n     - liveness age\n     - last status where available\n     - link to project page\n   - `S-fleet-index` is canonical and must be genuinely enacted.\n\n   Project summary:\n   - Render all available `state.json` fields:\n     - prompt reference\n     - direction in force\n     - clarity status\n     - budget\n     - criteria\n     - baseline\n     - builds and timestamps\n     - pending owner questions\n   - Missing `state.json` must render as a visible gap.\n\n   Comparison:\n   - Render sparse per-criterion line charts across cycles.\n   - No point where a cycle was not scored.\n   - Include a “show last N” depth picker anchored at the latest run.\n   - Always include the newest build in the selected comparison set.\n   - Clicking a point opens build detail.\n   - Render the conventions/scenarios matrix below the chart.\n   - Convention statuses:\n     - `conformed`\n     - `reckoned-departure`\n     - `silent-departure`\n     - `not-assessed`\n   - Scenario cells must include score and evidence class.\n   - Unchecked IDs must render as visible gaps, not pass or neutral.\n\n   Current state:\n   - Live-read convention/scenario ID sets and prompt revision from the source corpus.\n   - Keep this distinct from `state.json` snapshots.\n   - For the real project, the corpus path is `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\ProjectPrompt.md` and conventions path is `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`.\n\n   Build detail:\n   - Show timestamps.\n   - Show verdict JSON.\n   - Show evidence citations.\n   - Show launch pointer only for the most recent run.\n   - Older builds must show the pointer absent or stale.\n\n   Evidence:\n   - Create `evidence/scan-<timestamp>.log` from the real `-Once` run against `C:\\builds`.\n   - Include emitted fleet and project `data.js` payloads.\n   - Include sh