not copy corpus content wholesale into those locations.\n   - The project itself dogfoods the harness, so once a working build ships its shell is intended to be mirrored later into `C:\\Harness\\harness\\templates\\display/`.\n   - Prefer decisions over preference quizzes; no multiple-choice clarification was needed because the request fully specified the build.\n   - PowerShell 5.1 is the available PowerShell runtime; `pwsh` was unavailable.\n   - Python 3.12, Node 24, Edge, and Chrome were available for checks.\n   - The emitter needed UTF-8 BOM encoding because PowerShell 5.1 interpreted em-dashes/curly characters incorrectly under the default ANSI encoding.\n   - Short code excerpts only if later documenting work; cite repository paths and line numbers for larger code.\n\n5. Errors and Fixes:\n\n   - Initial emitter patch failed because the expected text did not match due to CRLF handling.\n     - Diagnosis: the generated file contained malformed `\\r\\r\\n` line endings.\n     - Fix: normalized the emitter to CRLF and applied patches through Python byte/text processing.\n\n   - A fixture-generation Python command failed with:\n     - `SyntaxError: unexpected character after line continuation character`\n     - Cause: incorrect escaping of a Windows path in a Python string.\n     - Fix: reran fixture creation with corrected path handling; fixtures were created successfully.\n\n   - Initial PowerShell parse check failed with:\n     - `Unexpected token 'root'`\n     - `Missing closing ')'`\n     - `The string is missing the terminator`\n     - Cause: PowerShell 5.1 parsing of the emitter file, compounded by encoding/quote issues.\n     - Fix: re-encoded the emitter with a UTF-8 BOM; subsequent parse check returned `parse ok`.\n\n   - First real emitter run failed:\n     - `Could not find a part of the path 'C:\\builds\\harness-ui\\display\\index.html'`\n     - Cause: destination project display directory was not created.\n     - Fix: added/used directory creation before copying shell files.\n\n   - Emitter then failed under `Set-StrictMode`:\n     - `The property 'conventions' cannot be found on this object.`\n     - Cause: optional properties were accessed directly on objects where they were absent.\n     - Fix: introduced a safe property accessor helper and patched risky accesses.\n\n   - Safe accessor initially used function name `GP`, which collided with PowerShell’s built-in `Get-ItemProperty` alias:\n     - Error: null path binding and incorrect behavior around `direction_in_force`.\n     - Fix: renamed the helper to avoid the alias collision.\n\n   - Emitter had an issue where `ConvertTo-Json` on a nested fleet object appeared to hang.\n     - Investigation showed the fleet serialization used the normal PowerShell serializer with a large nested object.\n     - Fix: replaced/adjusted serialization logic to use a custom JSON-safe serializer/path, after which the scan completed in about one second.\n\n   - Payload labels were initially wrong:\n     - `version\\s+(\\S+)` captured only `0` from strings such as `version 0.1`.\n     - `Re-score verdict` and `Verdict` heading regexes did not account for `:**`.\n     - Fix: changed version matching to numeric dotted versions and broadened heading parsing.\n\n   - Verdict heading labels became null:\n     - Cause: a second `-match` operation overwrote PowerShell’s automatic `$Matches` variable before the heading value was stored.\n     - Fix: stored the heading match result before performing subsequent regex matches.\n     - Correct output then included:\n       - `v0.1`\n       - `v0.2`\n       - `C1`\n       - `C1-rescore`\n       - `C2`\n       - `C3`\n       - `C4`\n\n   - Fleet serialization was instrumented with temporary debug markers:\n     - `payload serialize start`\n     - `payload serialize done`\n     - `fleetrow start`\n     - `fleetrow done`\n     - `fleet literal start`\n     - These markers helped isolate the hang and were intended to be removed or minimized after debugging.\n\n   - Initial render-check produced empty DOM files:\n     - `0 dom-fleet.html`\n     - `0 dom-project.html`\n     - Cause: headless invocation/check timing or output handling.\n     - Fix: reran the headless Edge dump; fleet DOM output then contained 1,970 bytes and full rendered rows.\n\n   - Fleet DOM output showed Windows paths rendered with backspace characters (`C:\builds`).\n     - This suggests the current custom string/JSON escaping code may be emitting `\\b` semantics incorrectly for backslashes.\n     - A final attempted patch to `ConvertTo-JsonEscape` failed because the exact multiline text did not match:\n       - `AssertionError`\n     - The most recent state is that the emitter still needs a careful review/fix of backslash escaping. The suspicious code region is around lines 463–465 of `version 0.1.0.001\\emitter\\harness-emit.ps1`, where the intended backslash replacement was not visibly distinct in the tool output.\n\n   - One scan command attempted to use Unix `ls`/`tail` against Windows paths and failed to find the wildcard path, but the evidence files were subsequently confirmed using directory listing.\n\n6. Problem Solving:\n\n   Solved:\n   - Established the required build directory structure.\n   - Implemented the emitter and static shell.\n   - Added fixture projects:\n     - `fixtures/fleet/stalerig`\n     - `fixtures/fleet/brokenrig`\n     - `fixtures/corpus/spec`\n   - Successfully discovered both real projects under `C:\\builds`.\n   - Successfully parsed:\n     - `harness-ui` state and scenario suite.\n     - `project` devlog, scenario suite, build folders, status files, and corpus metadata.\n   - Successfully emitted:\n     - `C:\\builds\\index.html`\n     - `C:\\builds\\data.js`\n     - `C:\\builds\\harness-ui\\display\\data.js`\n     - `C:\\builds\\project\\display\\data.js`\n   - Successfully rendered all major views under `file://` in headless Edge.\n   - Verified real-data counts and launch pointer behavior.\n   - Verified missing project state renders as a gap.\n   - Verified comparison charts and matrices are populated from the real corpus.\n\n   Ongoing:\n   - Review and correct custom JSON escaping so Windows paths remain valid strings and do not render `\\b` as a backspace.\n   - Re-run the real emitter after the escaping fix.\n   - Produce final `render-check.*` artifacts in the build’s evidence directory.\n   - Write the build manifest and scenario evidence/notes.\n   - Update the Cycle 1 `Result:` and `Time to implement` fields in `devlog.md`.\n   - Confirm temporary diagnostic logging does not remain unnecessarily in the final emitter run log.\n   - Confirm the deployed shell works with the final payload after all escaping changes.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\n   - Fix `ConvertTo-JsonEscape` in `version 0.1.0.001\\emitter\\harness-emit.ps1`, especially literal backslash handling.\n   - Validate emitted JSON with Node/Python and inspect path values.\n   - Run `-Once` again against `C:\\builds`.\n   - Capture the final `evidence\\scan-<timestamp>.log`.\n   - Copy or preserve final fleet/project payloads as evidence.\n   - Generate final render-check artifacts covering:\n     - fleet\n     - project summary\n     - comparison\n     - current state\n     - build detail\n     - stale refresh/liveness if possible\n   - Run fixture scans and record enactment-class scenario evidence.\n   - Write `build-manifest.md` with working behavior and declared absences.\n   - Write scenario evidence/notes.\n   - Update `devlog.md` Cycle 1:\n     - replace `**Time to implement:** session start ... <spawn>` with actual session start/end.\n     - replace `**Result:** <pending>` with the built artifact paths and evidence.\n     - leave `**Verdict:**` empty.\n   - Optionally remove temporary debug markers from the emitter after confirming they are no longer needed.\n   - Do not run a JEV or fill the verdict in this builder session.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Immediately before the pause, the implementation was in final validation/debugging.\n\n   Current build contents:\n   - `version 0.1.0.001\\emitter\\harness-emit.ps1` — 483 lines, PowerShell emitter.\n   - `version 0.1.0.001\\shell\\index.html`\n   - `version 0.1.0.001\\shell\\styles.css`\n   - `version 0.1.0.001\\shell\\harness.js` — approximately 586 lines, implementing the five views, SVG chart, matrices, refresh logic, and hash-based deep links.\n   - `version 0.1.0.001\\fixtures\\...`\n   - `version 0.1.0.001\\LAUNCH.md`\n   - `version 0.1.0.001\\launch.cmd`\n\n   The emitter has already successfully produced a final-looking scan log:\n   - `evidence\\scan-20261123-185109.log`\n   - Additional diagnostic scan logs include `scan-20261123-184848.log`, `scan-20261123-184851.log`, and `scan-20261123-184915.log`.\n\n   Most recent successful scan output included:\n   - `discovered 2 project(s): harness-ui, project`\n   - `harness-ui`: one entry, zero verdict JSON blocks, parsed state, 10 scenarios, one build.\n   - `project`: six entries, seven verdict JSON blocks, missing state.json rendered as a gap, 26 scenarios, two status files, four version folders, seven verdict series points.\n   - `project` corpus: prompt `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\ProjectPrompt.md`, conventions `C:\\Project\\MigrateInbound\\CONVENTIONS.md`, 56 convention IDs.\n   - `project\\display\\data.js` emitted at roughly 75 KB.\n   - Fleet `data.js` emitted at roughly 948 bytes.\n\n   Correct normalized verdict series:\n   - `v0.1` — `version 0.1 — Avatars`\n   - `v0.2` — `version 0.2 — GreyAvatar`\n   - `C1` — Cycle 1, build `version 0.3.0.001`\n   - `C1-rescore` — Cycle 1 rescore, build `version 0.3.0.001`\n   - `C2` — Cycle 2, build `version 0.3.0.002`\n   - `C3` — Cycle 3, build `version 0.3.0.003`\n   - `C4` — Cycle 4, build `version 0.3.0.004`\n\n   Headless render checks already demonstrated:\n   - Fleet table has two rows and all required columns.\n   - Comparison has 40 SVG circles/points.\n   - Scenario matrix has 182 cell