{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm re-examining the regex `[^\\s``\"']+?` and how it handles the backtick character. The content ` `stalerig` ` appears after `.md`, so the lazy match should stop before it. However, the `+?` requires at least one character. The match `C:\\b` proceeds as `\\` then `b`, but fails to match `\\.` with `u`. It continues until `0.1.0.001`, where it checks `\\.` and `(?:md|txt)`, failing on `.0`. It finally matches `Prompt.md`. I'm also checking if `Get-Content -Raw -Encoding UTF8` might be the issue, though it read fine in t4."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:53:57.737300+00:00"}}}}
