{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I've found the bug: my regex patterns `[^\\s``\"']+` and `\\S+` both fail on paths with spaces, like `C:\\builds\\harness-ui\\version 0.1.0.001`. The pattern `+?\\.(?:md|txt)` also fails because it stops at the first space. The fix is to match paths excluding newlines instead of all whitespace, allowing spaces within paths. This way, the lazy `+?` will correctly stop at the first `.md` or `.txt` extension."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-23T23:54:39.762163800+00:00"}}}}
