{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ubiquitous-eyebrow","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#46e6a6ba056c49818b8770257f7030cf","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"# Scenario suite — harness-ui line of development\n\nDerived at intake 2026-11-23 from `prompt.md`; **signed by owner 2026-11-23**. Each\nscenario scores 0–1 on the implementation's **ability to enact** it.\n\n## Scoring conventions\n\n- **Evidence class:** `enactment` (the emitter/shell ran or its artifacts demonstrate\n  the scenario) or `repository` (mechanism confirmed present — weaker).\n- **Score the outcome, not just the mechanism.** Rendered output must match the\n  derived data, not merely exist.\n- Test corpus: the real `C:\\builds\\project` line (4 cycles, verdicts, scenario suite,\n  status files) unless the direction names a fixture.\n\n## Suite\n\n| ID | Scenario | Exercises | Source |\n|----|----------|-----------|--------|\n| S-fleet-index | **Canonical.** `<root>/index.html` lists every machinery-carrying project — line, direction in force,\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nbudget spent, last verdict, liveness age — and links to each project page | discovery, summary | prompt §Views |\n| S-project-summary | Project page renders all `state.json` fields including pending owner questions | state render | p\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nompt §Views |\n| S-criteria-depth | Comparison chart renders per-criterion sparse lines; the depth picker limits to the last N cycles \u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\nnd always includes the latest | chart, selection | owner 2026-11-23 |\n| S-convention-matrix | Matrix shows per-id status per cycle; un-assessed ids render as visible gaps, never as pass | m\u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\ntrix, absence-as-finding | prompt §Views; H2 |\n| S-current-state | Current-state view shows the live corpus id set; a deliberately stale `state.json` snapshot shows a\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\n distinct from it | live-vs-snapshot | owner 2026-11-23 |\n| S-build-detail | Clicking a verdict point opens that build's detail: timestamps, verdict JSON, evidence citations | d\u001b[0mr\u001b[0m\nilldown | prompt §Views |\n| S-launch-pointer | The most recent build's detail shows a launcher pointer resolving to an existing artifact; older b\u001b[0mu\u001b[0m\nilds show it absent/stale | pointer, recency | owner 2026-11-23 |\n| S-stale-refresh | Refocusing the page reloads `data.js` only when a newer payload exists; visible pages poll on the 3\u001b[0m0\u001b[0m\ns timer | refresh | owner 2026-11-23 |\n| S-liveness-age | An idle project shows a growing liveness age; a file write under a watched path resets it on next sc\u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\nn | derivation | prompt §Architecture |\n| S-honest-absence | A project missing `state.json` or verdicts renders gaps, not fabricated values | honesty | prompt \u001b[0m§\u001b[0m\nConstraints |"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
